  "notes": "Funded-account rules are the only sane reason to tune a scalper this hard: 5% daily loss limit, 10% max drawdown, minimum trading days. Sized so a full loss day is ~1.2%, halted after 2 losers, everything flat before the window closes so nothing can gap through a limit. Deliberately slow. Also: slMaxPips 14 was refused by the break-even rail \u2014 the engine widens the stop to sit outside the range, and TP 6 against a 14p stop needs 75.3% even though the preset advertised 9. Capping the widening at 10p is the honest version of the same idea (69.4% needed, ceiling 70%).",
